{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "commonjs",
    "target": "ES2021",
    // sprint-4/sports-hub-highlightly-backend — adds "DOM" purely for its TYPE
    // declarations (fetch/Response/Headers/AbortController/RequestInit), not for any
    // runtime behavior. Needed because the installed @types/node@20.19.43 does not
    // ambiently type global `fetch` (confirmed directly — no `declare function fetch`
    // anywhere in node_modules/@types/node), even though the real Node runtime this app
    // requires (engines >=22.22.0) has had it natively since Node 18. The alternative —
    // adding a real HTTP client dependency (axios/got/undici) just to get types — would be
    // a heavier, unnecessary addition for a project whose every prior external-API
    // integration (Postmark, S3) already uses either a vendor SDK or, here, the runtime's
    // own built-in fetch. No existing file in this codebase uses a DOM-only global (window/
    // document/navigator) that this could silently redefine — verified via a clean
    // `nest build` + full test suite run after adding this line.
    "lib": ["ES2021", "DOM"],
    "declaration": true,
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "emitDecoratorMetadata": true,
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  // Sprint 1 / PR B1 is this project's first PR to add *.spec.ts files.
  // Without this, `nest build` (plain tsc under the hood) compiles test
  // files straight into the production dist/ output alongside real
  // source. jest.config.js points ts-jest at this same tsconfig for
  // *running* tests, so ts-jest still transforms *.spec.ts on its own
  // in-memory — only the production build output is affected.
  //
  // Sprint 2 / e2e-test-infrastructure added the "test" exclude below for
  // the same reason: this tsconfig has no "include", so TypeScript's
  // default file discovery starts from this file's own directory
  // (services/api/) and would otherwise pull services/api/test/*.ts
  // (including *.e2e-spec.ts) into `nest build`'s compilation too — and
  // fail on it, since "test" sits outside rootDir "./src". test/jest-e2e.
  // config.js's own ts-jest transform still runs those files fine for
  // `npm run test:e2e`, same "excluded from the build, not from testing"
  // split *.spec.ts already established.
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "test", "**/*.spec.ts"]
}
